  "scope": "Ordinary record_completed memory and SQLite policy over unchanged native admission, bounded codecs, sequence/group primitives, history/counter reads, writes and consuming immediate transactions.",
  "limitations": [
    "Frozen orchestration shares native codecs/storage and sequence/group primitives, not migrated ordinary-completion policy.",
    "Corrupt SQLite fixtures restore constraints before production calls. They are not valid recovery checkpoints or new dispatch authority.",
    "The low-level memory primitive checks sequence readiness first, accepts absent dispatches and replaces acknowledged terminals without clearing the lease field or adding image/proposal validation. Public VM entry still owns admission and authoritative winner replay.",
    "Durable native input admission precedes completed replay. Replay skips dispatch and sequence reads; pending completion checks native dispatch history and lease state before sequence readiness. Missing dispatches and raw non-completed states preserve released behavior, not new recovery admission.",
    "Public reopen cases inspect persisted member terminals separately from group-level visibility.",
    "Direct hooks model quota errors and uncertain commits/unwinds; native triggers and deferred constraints exercise rollback. No physical disk-full or power-loss experiment is claimed.",
    "No new Linux, remote CI, live GUI, standalone exported-source execution, full host-neutral durable recovery or throughput benchmark is claimed."
  ],
